\p{Agent AR1, 2026-11-24, 18:28Z - 19:30Z. No module code was changed or published. Everything of mine is under \code{\verb~|work/ar1/~} (distributions, reports, logs, scripts); living summary \code{\verb~|work/status/prof-AR1.md~}.}

\p{\strong{Framing (owner note 12).} The arena ranks by user-space instructions on Mathlib. That is the arena's metric, not the project's: the owner's target is warm wall clock (\code{\verb~|work/status/warm.md~}). This report says where the published code stands by the arena's rule and what the rule would reward; it is information, not a target. Instruction counts are exact and repeat to 0.2 \%; every wall-clock and CPU figure that is quoted as evidence was taken inside a \src{bench/quiet.py} window and is marked as such.}

\subtree{
\title{0. Tables first}

\subtree{
