\p{Every test that is not "correct" or a verdict on an \code{\verb~|either~} test, by name:}

\table{
\tr{\th{configuration}\th{test}\th{expected}\th{got}\th{cause}}
\tr{\td{(a), (b), (c*), (d)}\td{\code{\verb~|corner-cases/eta-struct-major-no-whnf~}, \code{\verb~|corner-cases/eta-struct-major-and-no-whnf~}}\td{either}\td{declined (exit 2)}\td{\code{\verb~|BUDGET_STEPS ...: the reduction returns to a term it started from; the official kernel does not terminate here~} (the published \code{\verb~|official~} row is a timeout on both). (a): 5 and 17 ms, 0.01 G instructions. (b), (d): 0.88 s and 24.0 G each, (c*): 1.85 s and 55.2 G each - the machine first runs into its own bound of 2^27 ticks per unit, then the reference engine declines}}
\tr{\td{(b)}\td{\code{\verb~|perf/loop-unfolded-once~}}\td{accept}\td{\strong{timeout} in the suite run (killed at the arena's 40 s); \strong{accepted in 31.6 s} when repeated alone in a quiet window (199.2 G instructions, 31.3 s CPU, \strong{8,686 MiB})}\td{not a wrong verdict. The machine works on one unit until its own tick bound cuts it, then the reference engine accepts the file (the reference engine alone: 76 ms, 1.5 G, 60 MiB; with the shortcuts of (d): 58 ms, 0.85 G). 31.6 s of a 40 s limit on this host's cores; the arena's runner is slower (nano-lean's Mathlib wall: 29.5 s here, 36.8 s published; gruszka 20.0 s and 32.5 s), so \strong{on the arena this test is a likely timeout with the machine's default switches}. With the candidate set (c*) it is accepted in 75 ms (0.77 G): \code{\verb~|same~} answers what the removed shortcuts used to}}
}

\p{No wrong accept and no wrong reject in any configuration. With (a) RLVM gives the published verdict of \code{\verb~|official~} (v4.35.0) on 268 of the 270 tests; the two others are the non-terminating \code{\verb~|either~} files above.}

\p{Note on (c*): at the time of the runs (19:14Z) the integrator's log (\code{\verb~|work/status/machine-INT6.log~}, entry of 19:06:35Z) calls NO switch set beyond the default "gated": it reports a candidate default with hostile exports and mutants clean, the full gate failing only on a harness artefact and re-gated on cedar + Std. Strictly, (c) is therefore skipped; (c*) is that candidate, run so that its arena figure exists when the integrator decides. It is not a gated configuration.}
}

