\p{Board (x86-64 G instructions): 1 nano-lean 394.9, 2 gruszka 462.0, 3 sokonanoda 527.4, 4 rpylean 578.1, 5 pestka 1,475.3, 6 kefir 2,577.3, 7 palladium 2,833.0, 8 con-ron 3,473.9, 9 kefir-wasm 3,496.0, 10 con-agua 3,925.9, 11 nanobruijn 4,704.7, 12 nanoda 5,773.3, 13 con-leche 6,133.9, 14 pestka-wasm 7,015.4, 15 tenet-jvm 9,798.4, 16 official-nightly 9,815.1, 17 eink0rn 10,611.2, 18 official 12,095.3.}

\p{What costs places: nothing but the Mathlib count. The sort key is (bad tests accepted, good tests rejected, Mathlib instructions, declined count); RLVM has 0 / 0 in every configuration, so its place is its Mathlib count, and the 2 or 3 declines / timeouts only break an exact tie in instructions. A single wrong reject would put the entry behind all 27 checkers that have neither (place 28), a single wrong accept behind the 29 that have no wrong accept (place 30), whatever the speed.}
}

