\tr{\td{10}\td{items 1 + 3 + 4 + 6 + 7 (+ the part of item 2 that survives the shortcuts)}\td{-}\td{-}\td{sum}\td{about 1,500 - 1,650 G}\td{\strong{6}; place 5 needs 1,339.6 G: another 160 - 310 G (10 - 19 \%) that nothing in sight provides}}
\tr{\td{11}\td{place 4 (rpylean: 544.4 G here)}\td{with a leader-class loader and admission (43 G) the checking would have to cost 500 G = 1.3 x gruszka's 381 G; the machine's checking is 2,820 G in (b) (7.4 x) and 1,819 G in (d) (4.8 x)}\td{about -1,000 G after row 10}\td{-}\td{544 G}\td{4: needs the cost per machine operation (2,133 instructions per tick against gruszka's 823, 1.5 x its ticks; P8 section 4.6) to fall by a factor of about 3 ON TOP of the shortcuts}}
}

\p{Reading: making the machine the default is worth seven places (15 -> 8). After that the only single step that moves a place for certain is the shortcut policy (8 -> 6). The candidate switch set is worth 7.7 \% on Mathlib and stays 8th (7th only at the edge of the projection range); with everything official-exact that exists or is being prototyped the entry reaches 7th. Places 5 and better are not reachable by switching on anything that exists: they need the per-operation cost.}
}

\subtree{
\title{0.5 The arena definition (\code{\verb~|scripts/arena/rlvm.yaml~}): what the integrator has to update}

\p{Checked, fine: valid against the arena's schema; the run line works under \code{\verb~|sh -c~} (dash) with \code{\verb~|$IN~} and maps 10 / 11 / 12 to 0 / 1 / 2 (exercised 270 x 4 times here); \code{\verb~|threads: 4~} = \code{\verb~|--threads 4~}; \code{\verb~|version: "0.1.0-SNAPSHOT"~} = the first line of \code{\verb~|rlvm --version~}; the build uses GraalVM CE only (\code{\verb~|--no-pgo~}; builder banner "GraalVM CE 25.5.5.0.3+1.1"; the cached tarball has the pinned sha256 \code{\verb~|41741c06...~}); the eight third-party jars on the image class path match \code{\verb~|scripts/arena/deps.sha256~} in both builds of this session; the \code{\verb~|build:~} line run in a clean copy of the tree \strong{without network} succeeds (section 8).}

\p{To do before submission:}

\ol{
\li{\code{\verb~|url~}, \code{\verb~|ref~}, \code{\verb~|rev~} are placeholders (\code{\verb~|https://example.invalid/rlvm.git~}, \code{\verb~|main~}, \code{\verb~|"0000000"~}): set them to the public repository, its branch and the full commit hash. The arena fetches exactly that commit with depth 1, so the commit must contain \code{\verb~|pom.xml~}, \code{\verb~|env.sh~}, \code{\verb~|scripts/~} and all 15 modules.}
\li{\strong{The arena build is a tree build and puts \code{\verb~|rlvm-testkit~} on the image class path} (23 jars), which no distribution that anybody gates or measures has (\code{\verb~|scripts/build.sh --published~}: 22 jars). The image still lists the engines \code{\verb~|machine, reference*~} and gives the right verdicts, but it is not the gated binary. Either leave the test kit out of the arena image or gate a tree-built image.}
\li{The header comment is stale: it describes the wave-5 state (14 modules; "nothing is checked with \verb~|[~the machine\verb~|]~ yet" is still true, but the machine's default switch set, its own tick bound, the eager-reduction fallback, \code{\verb~|rlvm-truffle~} in the parent pom since 18:16Z and the versioned \code{\verb~|work/dist~} link are not in it). "All 230 published tests correct (0 declined)" should read: 270 of 270 without a wrong verdict, 2 \code{\verb~|either~} tests declined.}
\li{When the machine becomes the default engine: rewrite the second paragraph of \code{\verb~|description~} (it says the reference engine checks every declaration), say that units the machine declines are checked by the reference engine, and first settle \code{\verb~|perf/loop-unfolded-once~} (0.1: 31.6 s of a 40 s limit here, 8.7 GB) - with the default switches the change of engine trades a correct verdict for a probable timeout on the arena's slower runner; the candidate set (c*) does settle it (75 ms).}
\li{Not pinned by hash: the Maven plugins and their dependencies (an 88 MB local repository; only \code{\verb~|--strict-checksums~} against the repository's own checksum files). The description's sentence "verifies their checksums and those of the third-party jars that go into the image" is accurate, but the build is not hermetic. If that matters, add a hash list for the plugin set or vendor the repository.}
\li{Decide M6's request of 17:12Z (H10 inline lists in the native-image build, \src{rlvm-machine/h10/native-image-args.sh}): it is not in \src{scripts/build.sh}; if adopted, the build line of the arena image changes and needs its own end-to-end run.}
\li{\code{\verb~|threads: 4~} is a wall-clock choice only; it does not move the ranking metric measurably for the leaders (research 12, section 4) and was not re-measured for RLVM today. If the owner's 8 workers / pipelined load (P7-F4) become the launcher's default, change BOTH numbers and run this procedure again: the arena's limits are per test and \code{\verb~|perf/~} tests are single units.}
\li{Observation, not verified further: the pinned COMMUNITY tarball itself ships modules with "enterprise" in their names (\code{\verb~|com.oracle.graal.graal_enterprise~}, \code{\verb~|com.oracle.svm.svm_enterprise~}, ... in \code{\verb~|jmods/~} and in the \code{\verb~|MODULES~} line of \code{\verb~|release~}; \code{\verb~|IMPLEMENTOR="GraalVM Community"~}, GPL licence file). Nothing was downloaded or changed by me; the Oracle GraalVM directory \code{\verb~|.toolchain/oracle-graalvm-25~} is not touched by any build of this session.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{0.6 What could not be established}

\ul{
\li{\strong{RLVM's own aarch64 / x86-64 ratio.} Every place above is a projection. (b) is 8th for every ratio a baseline has shown, but at the 1.05 edge it is 4 G (0.13 \%) behind palladium, and (c*) is 7th there.}
\li{\strong{Wall clock of \code{\verb~|perf/loop-unfolded-once~} on the arena's runner} with the machine: 31.6 s here in a quiet window; the runner's speed is only known through the leaders' published wall times.}
\li{\strong{A gated configuration (c).} The integrator's log calls no set beyond the default gated; (c*) is its candidate.}
\li{\strong{The size of item 3 and item 5} of table 0.4: E1 and C1 are prototypes; the fallback's share is an estimate from class names in a sampled profile (290 - 350 G), not a per-unit measurement.}
\li{\strong{The arena build on the arena's runner}: whether its nix shell has \code{\verb~|curl~} / \code{\verb~|wget~} and a C compiler that links \code{\verb~|-lz~} (the flake lists neither \code{\verb~|zlib~} nor \code{\verb~|curl~}; the build has a zlib-from-source path, which downloads). The online path (Maven Central, the GraalVM tarball) was not exercised by me: no downloads were allowed. The last online run is the steward's of 12:40Z.}
\li{\strong{Whether the arena counts kernel instructions too} (research 01, section 1.2). If it does: (a) +208.9 G (2.5 \%), (b) +29.5 G (1.0 \%), nano-lean +4.9 G; no place changes.}
\li{\strong{Thread count against instructions for RLVM} (4 against 8 workers, batch against pipelined): not measured.}
\li{Wall and CPU of (d) on Mathlib: measured outside a window (162 s / 168 s on a parked container) and not quoted.}
}
}
