}

\p{The load is 1.6 \% of (a), 4.5 \% of (b), 6.7 \% of (d), and 37 \% of nano-lean's WHOLE run.}
}

\subtree{
\title{6.2 By thread and module (\code{\verb~|perf record -e instructions:u -c N~}, all threads, in the container)}

\p{Profile image \code{\verb~|work/ar1/dist-sym~}: the same jars and flags plus \code{\verb~|-H:-DeleteLocalSymbols~}; 167,969 samples of 50 M instructions for (a), 149,103 samples of 20 M for (b). Native-image symbols carry no package, so classes are mapped to their jar by simple name (\code{\verb~|work/ar1/scripts/prof-class.py~}); \code{\verb~|IntIntMap~} exists in two jars.}

\table{
\tr{\th{}\th{(a) reference engine: 8,398.5 G sampled}\th{(b) machine: 2,982.1 G sampled}}
\tr{\td{worker threads (checking)}\td{8,239.6 G (98.1 \%)}\td{2,822.4 G (94.6 \%)}}
\tr{\td{main thread (reader + loader)}\td{133.1 G (1.6 \%)}\td{133.1 G (4.5 \%)}}
\tr{\td{environment thread (admission)}\td{25.8 G (0.3 \%)}\td{26.6 G (0.9 \%)}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|rlvm-machine~}}\td{-}\td{2,378.6 G (79.8 \%): \code{\verb~|Values~} 855.0 G, \code{\verb~|Eval~} 776.7 G, \code{\verb~|Infer~} 274.9 G, \code{\verb~|Conv~} 119.4 G, \code{\verb~|Runs~} 97.1 G, \code{\verb~|Levels~} 60.6 G, \code{\verb~|Machine~} 60.6 G, \code{\verb~|Reduce~} 55.6 G, \code{\verb~|Pairs~} 37.6 G}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|rlvm-store~} (hash-consed terms: interning, substitution, memo tables)}\td{6,092.8 G (72.5 \%): \code{\verb~|Overlay~} 2,588.7 G, \code{\verb~|TermOps$Rewriter~} 1,567.8 G, \code{\verb~|Terms~} 936.6 G, \code{\verb~|TermOps$Memo~} 690.1 G, \code{\verb~|NodeCtx~} 223.8 G}\td{378.0 G (12.7 \%; 320.6 G on worker threads): \code{\verb~|Overlay~} 111.6 G, \code{\verb~|Rewriter~} 76.2 G, \code{\verb~|Terms~} 65.3 G, \code{\verb~|NodeCtx~} 31.3 G, \code{\verb~|Memo~} 26.4 G, \code{\verb~|ProofBlocks~} 37.7 G}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|rlvm-ref~} (+ \code{\verb~|IntIntMap~})}\td{1,179.8 G + 824.5 G (23.9 \%)}\td{43.7 G + 36.0 G (2.7 \%)}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|rlvm-export~} + \code{\verb~|rlvm-load~} (reader, loader)}\td{88.9 G (1.1 \%)}\td{85.4 G (2.9 \%)}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|rlvm-level~}, \code{\verb~|rlvm-api~}}\td{178.7 G (2.1 \%)}\td{40.0 G (1.3 \%)}}
\tr{\td{\strong{garbage collector} (\code{\verb~|com.oracle.svm.core.genscavenge~})}\td{\strong{8.7 G (0.1 \%)}}\td{\strong{0.6 G (0.0 \%)}}}
\tr{\td{other Substrate VM runtime (array copies), JDK code, libc, vdso, no symbol}\td{21.2 G (0.3 \%)}\td{15.4 G (0.5 \%)}}
\tr{\td{JIT compiler}\td{none: the image is compiled ahead of time; no compiler thread exists}\td{none}}
}

\p{Top symbols, (a): \code{\verb~|Overlay.mkApp~} 21.7 \%, \code{\verb~|TermOps$Rewriter.leaf~} 9.9 \%, \code{\verb~|Rewriter.run~} 8.7 \%, \code{\verb~|IntIntMap.get~} 7.1 \%, \code{\verb~|TermOps$Memo.put~} 5.8 \%, \code{\verb~|Terms.kind~} 5.1 \%; the kernel's own control code (\code{\verb~|RefKernel.*~}) is 13.7 \%. (b): \code{\verb~|Values.neu~} 8.0 \%, \code{\verb~|Values.closureProbe~} 5.3 \%, \code{\verb~|Eval.argvFast~} 4.3 \%, \code{\verb~|Eval.app~} 4.0 \%, \code{\verb~|Eval.gate~} 4.0 \%, \code{\verb~|Values.frameProbe~} 3.8 \%, \code{\verb~|Values.closureOverNew~} 2.9 \%, \code{\verb~|Values.mkConst~} 2.8 \%. Full tables: \code{\verb~|work/ar1/prof/a.tables.md~}, \code{\verb~|b.tables.md~}; raw sums per symbol: \code{\verb~|a.syms.tsv~}, \code{\verb~|b.syms.tsv~}.}

\p{In the arena's currency the collector is nothing (the stores are primitive arrays), there is no JIT to pay for, and reading the file is the only fixed cost of any size. For the reference engine three quarters of all instructions are interning and substitution in the term store; for the machine 80 \% are its own value store and evaluator, which is the per-operation cost of P8's section 4.6.}
}

\subtree{
\title{6.3 The eager-reduction fallback inside (b)}

\p{\code{\verb~|-X machine.declines~} of the profile run lists 13,422 declines = \strong{6,711 units, each declined twice} (\code{\verb~|UNSUPPORTED_INPUT (E_LIMIT) ... eager reduction~}), as P8 counted. Those units are checked by the reference engine. On the worker threads of (b) the classes that carry the reference engine in (a) (\code{\verb~|RefKernel~}, \code{\verb~|PairSet~}, \code{\verb~|LongIntMap~}, \code{\verb~|IntIntMap~}, \code{\verb~|Overlay~}, \code{\verb~|TermOps$Rewriter~}, \code{\verb~|TermOps$Memo~}) sum to 287 G; in (a) the same classes are 83 \% of the workers' instructions, so the fallback is about \strong{290 - 350 G, 10 - 12 \% of (b)}, for units that cost gruszka 23.9 G (P8). This is an estimate from class names, not a per-unit count: if the machine itself calls into the term store's interner, it is too high. Cross-check: P8 measured 23.5 s of thread CPU for the fallback; at the reference engine's 13.5 G instructions per CPU second (table 0.2) that is 317 G.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{7. What it would take: how table 0.4 was made}

\ul{
\li{Items 1, 2 and 4 are measured end to end with the arena's procedure (tables 0.1 - 0.3).}
\li{Item 3: fallback of 6.3 (290 - 350 G) plus the machine's abandoned attempts (15.3 G, P8 section 4.3) minus what the machine would spend on those units at its present ratio to gruszka (6.5 x 23.9 G = 155 G; 3.9 x with the shortcuts = 93 G).}
\li{Item 5 (C1) has no number: it aims at the comparisons that item 4 removes while keeping the official verdict.}
\li{Items 6 and 7 are bounds: today's count minus the leaders' for the same phase.}
\li{Rows 9 and 10 add the items; savings measured on different switch sets do not add exactly, so they are rounded and carry the uncertainty of item 3.}
\li{Row 11 uses research 12 (gruszka reads for 37.5 G and checks for 381 G) and P8 (after the shortcuts the machine is at 1.5 x gruszka's ticks and 2.6 x its instructions per tick).}
\li{Not in the table because they are not instruction items: the worker count, pipelined loading, heap sizing (\code{\verb~|-Xms~}), the collector choice. They move wall clock, which the board shows and does not rank.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{8. The arena definition, run end to end from a clean copy without network}

\p{\code{\verb~|work/ar1/scripts/e2e.sh~}: a clean copy of the tree as of 18:38:38Z (parent pom, \code{\verb~|env.sh~}, \code{\verb~|scripts/~}, the 15 modules without \code{\verb~|target/~}; 1,231 files) in \code{\verb~|work/ar1/e2e/src~}; its \code{\verb~|.toolchain~} = links to the pinned GraalVM CE and Maven of the host and a COPY of the third-party part of \code{\verb~|.toolchain/m2~} (no \code{\verb~|rlvm~} artifact); then, in the arena image with \code{\verb~|--no-network~}, 8 CPUs, 16 GB:}

\pre{\verb~|
sh -c "scripts/arena/build.sh"        # the build: line of rlvm.yaml
~}

\p{Result: status 0 after 513 s. Maven built all 15 modules in 12.6 s (the whole tree compiles); the third-party jars match \code{\verb~|deps.sha256~}; the JVM launcher and the image passed the build's verification (exit-status protocol, Truffle probe); native-image \code{\verb~|-O3~} 496 s wall, 1,067 s CPU, peak 3.8 GB; \code{\verb~|work/dist~} is a link into \code{\verb~|work/dist.d/20261124T185419Z-d7be406ab8dd-native~} and the run line resolves through it; \code{\verb~|bin/rlvm~} 66,062,456 bytes (sha256 \code{\verb~|7ca470b6ae5a...~}), dynamic dependencies libz, libc. Then (\code{\verb~|work/ar1/scripts/e2e-check.sh~}, same image, no network): the yaml validates against \code{\verb~|refs/lean-kernel-arena/schemas/checker.json~}; the run line gives accept on \code{\verb~|init-prelude~} (0.95 G instructions), \code{\verb~|tutorial/001_basicDef~}, \code{\verb~|perf/app-lam~} (55.3 G) and \code{\verb~|init~} (245.1 G), reject on \code{\verb~|tutorial/002_badDef~} and \code{\verb~|corner-cases/imax-right-successor~}.}

\p{Tree against published jars (class files compared by name and CRC): identical for admit, api, cli, driver, export, inductive, level, machine, main, nat, ref; \strong{different for rlvm-load, rlvm-store and rlvm-truffle} (the tree is ahead of the published jars: LP2 and T3 at work); \code{\verb~|rlvm-testkit~} only in the tree build. On \code{\verb~|init~} the tree-built image needs 245.1 G against 246.3 G for the published jars (-0.45 \%).}

\p{What this does and does not show: with the pinned toolchain and a Maven repository that already holds the plugins, nothing else is fetched and the build is reproducible offline; that the downloads themselves work was not tested here.}
}

\subtree{
\title{9. Known open items: can they show on the arena's test set?}

\table{
\tr{\th{item (board, \code{\verb~|work/status/requests.log~})}\th{on today's 270 tests}\th{if it showed}}
\tr{\td{A2-F1: two level records for one universe parameter - RLVM accepts files that the official checker rejects}\td{no: 0 of the 270 files and none of the eight corpora contain a repeated level record (A2's scanner over the 230 published tests and the corpora; the 30 \code{\verb~|either~} tests and the two extra \code{\verb~|perf/~} tests scanned for this report)}\td{a hand-made \code{\verb~|bad~} test of that shape would be a WRONG ACCEPT: place 30 whatever the speed. The only open item that can cost the whole ranking, so it should be closed (decline is enough) before any submission}}
\tr{\td{the \code{\verb~|either~} tests}\td{all 30 answered or declined; verdicts = \code{\verb~|official~} on 28}\td{free: \code{\verb~|either~} never counts}}
\tr{\td{the two non-terminating \code{\verb~|either~} files with the machine (orchestrator 16:14Z)}\td{declined after 0.88 s and 24 G each (the machine's tick bound of 16:45Z, then the reference engine); the arena's limit is 60 s}\td{closed for the arena}}
\tr{\td{the machine's tick bound on a \code{\verb~|good~} test: \code{\verb~|perf/loop-unfolded-once~}}\td{(b): timeout at 40 s in the suite run, accepted in 31.6 s in a quiet window (199 G, 8.7 GB). (c*): accepted in 75 ms (0.77 G); (d): 58 ms}\td{a timeout = one more "declined": no place lost, a red cell on a test that the reference engine passes in 76 ms}}
\tr{\td{eager-reduction declines of the machine}\td{unit-level only: the reference engine decides those units, no test is declined for it; 6,711 units on Mathlib}\td{costs instructions (0.4, item 3), never a verdict}}
\tr{\td{generated constants (admission declines an export that needs a kernel-generated constant without a record)}\td{0 of 270: no test is declined for it}\td{a decline: tie-breaker only}}
\tr{\td{the machine is not the default (\code{\verb~|MachineProvider.priority()~} = 10)}\td{the definition as it is runs the reference engine: place 15 instead of 8}\td{seven places}}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{10. Reproduction and files}

\pre{\verb~|
# distribution from the published jars, arena flags (5-6 min; one of the host's two native-image slots)
bench/slot.sh -c ni -n 2 -- scripts/build.sh --published --no-pgo --opt 3 \
    --verify-deps scripts/arena/deps.sha256 --dist work/ar1/dist
mkdir -p work/ar1/src/work && ln -sfn ../../dist work/ar1/src/work/dist
RUN="$(sed -n 's/^run:[[:space:]]*//p' scripts/arena/rlvm.yaml | head -n 1)"
work/ar1/scripts/suite.sh a "$RUN"                                  # all 270 tests, report work/ar1/reports/a.json
work/ar1/scripts/one.sh --quiet mathlib-a-quiet work/exports/mathlib.ndjson 4120 "$RUN"   # Mathlib in a quiet window
bench/slot.sh -- bench/quiet.py -- work/ar1/scripts/leaders.sh gruszka nano-lean sokonanoda
python3 -I work/ar1/scripts/tables.py a b c d                        # verdict and cost tables
python3 -I work/ar1/scripts/mathlib-table.py                         # Mathlib table and projection
python3 -I work/ar1/board.py --row "rlvm:0:0:3.256e12:3"             # the board with a hypothetical row
# phases, profile
work/ar1/scripts/one.sh mathlib-stop-load work/exports/mathlib.ndjson 4120 'work/dist/bin/rlvm --threads 4 -X stop-after=load "$IN"'
bench/slot.sh -c ni -n 2 -- work/ar1/scripts/build-sym.sh            # the same jars with symbols: work/ar1/dist-sym
bench/slot.sh -- bench/arena-docker.sh --arena-limits --no-network work/ar1/scripts/prof-in.sh \
    $PWD/work/ar1/prof/b 20000000 -- $PWD/work/ar1/dist-sym/bin/rlvm --threads 4 -X engine=machine $PWD/work/exports/mathlib.ndjson
python3 -I work/ar1/scripts/prof-class.py work/ar1/prof/b.syms.tsv   # one perf record at a time (the ring buffers are per user)
# the arena build line from a clean copy, no network
work/ar1/scripts/e2e.sh && bench/arena-docker.sh --arena-limits --no-network work/ar1/scripts/e2e-check.sh
~}

\p{Files: \code{\verb~|work/ar1/reports/{a,b,c,d}.json~} (every test: status, exit code, instructions, times, RSS, the checker's output), \code{\verb~|tables-*.md~}, \code{\verb~|mathlib-*-quiet.json~}, \code{\verb~|leader-*.json~}, \code{\verb~|loop-b-quiet.json~}, \code{\verb~|mathlib-stop-*.json~}; \code{\verb~|work/ar1/logs/~} (suite logs, run lines, jar hashes, the offline build's log \code{\verb~|e2e-build.log~}, \code{\verb~|e2e-check.log~}); \code{\verb~|work/ar1/prof/~} (profiles; \code{\verb~|b.declines.txt~}: the machine's declines on Mathlib).}
}
